cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, and cite the datasets it analyses as their publishers ask (see references)."
type: software
title: "Soil Carbon Kriging: soil organic carbon mapped with its uncertainty, in Python"
abstract: >-
  Bayesian kriging of field-scale soil organic carbon stocks (0-30 cm) at
  1,163 locations in eight U.S. Midwest fields, with REML covariance models,
  terrain covariates from USGS 3DEP, cross-validation against two random
  forests, maps with their predictive uncertainty, and each field's mean
  stock by Bayesian block kriging with the samples needed to detect a change.
  Each stage's acceptance rules are fixed by a commit before its data is used.
authors:
